cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. Research prototype, not a medical device:
  see DISCLAIMER.md.
type: software
title: "ptsd-eeg-prototype: a nested-LOSO resting-EEG pipeline and an honest negative result"
version: 4.1.1
license: MIT
authors:
  - given-names: "Bogdan"
    alias: "zititank"
    website: "https://github.com/zititank"
  - alias: "AdetyTy"
    website: "https://github.com/AdetyTy"
  - alias: "Qwertyqwerty579"
    website: "https://github.com/Qwertyqwerty579"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zititank/ptsd-eeg-prototype"
url: "https://github.com/zititank/ptsd-eeg-prototype"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible pipeline that scores a one-minute, eyes-closed recording from a 6-channel consumer EEG headband
  for similarity to a PTSD cohort: four occipital spectral features, shrinkage LDA, a 90-member nested
  leave-one-subject-out ensemble and a pre-registered decision rule. The headline AUC is explained by an
  acquisition artefact in one control batch; against valid controls the model performs at chance. The data are
  confidential and not included; the repository ships code, pickle-free weights, aggregate model metrics and a
  synthetic demo.
keywords:
  - EEG
  - PTSD
  - resting state
  - alpha rhythm
  - nested cross-validation
  - leave-one-subject-out
  - pre-registration
  - negative result
